whoa dude everybody's favorite actor  kiana reeves recently took part in an  interview with siriusxm  accompanied by his buddy and bill and  ted based the music co-star alex winter  asked if there were any characters he  wished he could travel back in time to  play  reeves didn't hesitate to name drop a  certain grizzled canadian adamantium  infused mutant  as reeves put it i always want to play  wolverine  winter who didn't seem at all surprised  by this immediately chimed in with  it's not too late it is too late it's  not too late for kiara to play wolverine  i'm just going to leave  that there reeves though disagree saying  it's too late the role has been filled  really well and i'm all good with it now  reeves likely knew that what he was  saying was going to send x-men fans into  a tizzy  the x fandom has long linked the actor  with that particular role and when it  came time for hugh jackman to step down  from the park speculation ignited anew  that marvel might take a look at reeves  to play the next iteration of wolverine  in the marvel cinematic universe  of course there's probably no way that  will happen following disney's  acquisition of fox marvel studios boss  kevin feige is taking over the x-men  movie franchise and is reportedly  looking to recast wolverine with a  younger actor  with the potential exception of deadpool  the entire x-men lineup will likely be  recast with younger stars reeves is  almost a whole 4 years older than  jackman who's in his early 50s making  his chances of playing a wolverine slim  to none  unless marvel wanted to employ him for  flash forward sequences at some point  just to be clear though reeves didn't  bring up wolverine just a toy with fans  hearts  when asked to confirm that he was  serious about his pining for the role  the actor said quote  oh yeah frank miller's wolverine for  sure there are about a million reasons  why frank miller is a comics legend and  for marvel the writer and artist did  some of his most tremendous work  in the early 80s miller successfully  rebooted daredevil  many of the traits we now take for  granted about matt murdock his strong  moral code his catholicism his tortured  inner battle over his crime-fighting  career or miller's doing  in 1982 miller and the equally legendary  comics writer chris claremont were  sharing a cab on the way back from san  diego comic-con when they conceived the  idea for a four-part mini-series  centered on wolverine the x-man who had  swiftly risen to become one of marvel's  most popular characters since his 1974  introduction  thanks to claremont's stark writing and  miller's kinetic expertly laid out  panels the miniseries which ran from  september to december 1982 became a  massive hit  the series did for james howlett aka  logan what miller's daredevil run had  done for matt murdock  strongly establishing his  characterization motivations and  backstory in a way that would come to  define him for decades  doing a little quick math reeves would  have just turned 18 years old when the  debut issue of miller's wolverine  dropped in 1982 so we can't say we're  surprised it had a lasting effect on it  unfortunately as reeves himself noted  that ship has pretty much sailed  while that doesn't mean the chances of  seeing him in the mcu in some capacity  are totally squashed  marvel enthusiasts have been fan casting  reeves in all kinds of mcu roles for  years now and if there's one thing we  know about kevin feige it's that he's  keen to give the fans what they want  last summer during the press tour for  spider-man far from home  feige was asked if reeves had ever been  considered for a role in a marvel flick  feige replied we talk to him for almost  every film we make  i don't know when if or ever he'll join  the mcu but we very much want to figure  out the right way to do it  feige wasn't just whistling dixie he  went on to compare the situation with  reeves with a casting of jake gyllenhaal  with whom he said marvel had also spoken  about a bevy of different roles before  he was finally cast as quentin beck  aka mysterio and far from home so while  reeves may not be suiting up as  wolverine we're pretty sure that sooner  or later feige will find a way to bring  the world's most beloved actor into the  world's biggest movie franchise  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

